  "stemZh": "您有一个 Microsoft Foundry 项目，用于处理供应商提交的采购文档。\n您需要使用 Foundry Tools 中的 Azure 内容理解实现两个管道。该解决方案必须满足以下要求：\n包括一个名为 Pipeline1 的管道，支持经济高效、高容量处理独立的 PDF 发票。\n包括一个名为 Pipeline2 的管道，支持通过多步骤推理和参考数据进行跨文档验证。\n您应该如何配置每个管道？要回答这个问题，请将适当的配置拖动到正确的管道中。每个配置可以使用一次、使用多次或根本不使用。您可能需要拖动窗格之间的分隔条或滚动以查看内容。\n注意： 每个正确的选择值为一分。\n选择和放置：",
  "stemEn": "You have a Microsoft Foundry project that processes procurement documents submitted by suppliers.\nYou need to implement two pipelines by using Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools. The solution must meet the following requirements:\nInclude a pipeline named Pipeline1 that supports cost-effective, high-volume processing of standalone PDF invoices.\nInclude a pipeline named Pipeline2 that supports cross-document validation by using multi-step reasoning and reference data.\nHow should you configure each pipeline? To answer, drag the appropriate configurations to the correct pipelines. Each configuration may be used once, more than once, of not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.\nSelect and Place:",
  "explanationZh": "框1：以标准模式运行的单文件任务\n管道1\n为了满足使用 Azure 内容理解在 Foundry 工具中处理独立 PDF 发票的成本效益高的高容量处理管道的要求，您应该将管道配置为以标准模式运行的单文件任务。\n1. 任务类型：单文件任务\n该场景涉及处理独立的 PDF 发票。单文件任务旨在独立处理单个文件，逐个提取结构化字段。\n何时避免多文件：多文件任务旨在用于高级用例，在这些用例中，您需要在单个请求中传递多个不同的文档，以交叉引用数据、汇总统计信息或运行复杂的跨文件验证逻辑。将其用于高容量独立提取会增加不必要的技术开销。\n2. 分析模式：标准模式\n标准模式明确强调成本效益和降低延迟。它针对从单个文档中提取简单字段（例如收集发票号码、日期、行项目和总额）进行了优化。\n成本差异：标准模式的上下文化令牌定价较低（每百万个令牌 $1.00），相比之下专业模式为每百万个令牌 $1.50。\n何时避免专业模式：专业模式是为多步骤推理、进行推断和将输入文件与预先上传的知识库/参考数据进行比较而构建的。对于简单的大量提取，专业模式增加了不必要的成本和延迟。\n框2：专业模式下的多文件任务\nPipeline2\n要在Azure内容理解中使用多步骤推理和参考数据实现跨文档验证，您的管道必须配置为专业模式下的多文件任务。\n以下是为什么需要这种确切配置的详细说明：\n1. 任务类型：多文件任务\n单任务（单文件任务）配置仅限于每个请求处理一个孤立文档。\n能力：多文件任务允许Azure内容理解在单个请求中接受多个输入文件，使系统能够集体推理、验证结果并在不同文档之间聚合模式。\n2. 处理模式：专业模式\n标准模式严格用于从单个文件中进行简单字段提取，而没有复杂的认知负担。\n能力：专业模式解锁了高级生成AI代理能力。它允许您注入外部知识库作为参考数据，进行多步骤语义推理，并执行跨文档数据验证，以在生成最终统一模式之前标记错误。\nfoundry-classic",
  "explanationEn": "Box 1: Single-file task running in Standard mode\nPipeline1\nTo meet the requirements for a cost-effective, high-volume processing pipeline of standalone PDF invoices using Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools, you should configure the pipeline with a Single-file task running in Standard mode.\n1. Task Type: Single-file task\nThe scenario involves processing standalone PDF invoices. A Single-file task is designed to process individual files independently, drawing structured field extractions schema-by-schema.\nWhen to avoid Multi-file: Multi-file tasks are intended for advanced use cases where you need to pass multiple distinct documents in a single request to cross-reference data, aggregate statistics, or run complex cross-file validation logic. Using it for high-volume standalone extraction would add unnecessary technical overhead.\n2. Analysis Mode: Standard mode\nStandard mode explicitly emphasizes cost-effectiveness and reduced latency. It is optimized for straightforward field extraction (such as gathering invoice numbers, dates, line items, and totals) from individual documents.\nCost Difference: Standard mode features lower pricing for Contextualization tokens ($1.00 per 1M tokens) compared to Pro mode ($1.50 per 1M tokens).\nWhen to avoid Pro mode: Pro mode is built for multi-step reasoning, drawing inferences, and comparing input files against a pre-uploaded knowledge base/reference data. For simple high-volume extraction, Pro mode adds unnecessary cost and latency.\nBox 2: Multi-file task in Pro mode\nPipeline2\nTo implement cross-document validation using multi-step reasoning and reference data in Azure Content Understanding, your pipeline must be configured as a Multi-file task in Pro mode.\nHere is the breakdown of why this exact configuration is required:\n1. Task Type: Multi-file task\nSingle-task (Single-file task) configurations are restricted to processing one isolated document per request.\nCapability: A Multi-file task allows Azure Content Understanding to accept multiple input files in a single request, enabling the system to collectively reason, validate results, and aggregate schemas across distinct documents.\n2. Processing Mode: Pro Mode\nStandard mode is built strictly for straightforward field extraction from single files without complex cognitive overhead.\nCapability: Pro mode unlocks advanced generative AI agentic capabilities. It allows you to inject an external knowledge base for reference data, run multi-step semantic reasoning, and perform cross-document data validation to flag errors before producing a final unified schema.\nfoundry-classic",
