  "stemZh": "您有一个 Microsoft Foundry 项目，其中包含基于内部文档的客户支持代理。\n在最近的更新后，用户报告了以下问题：\n一些答案没有被检索到的文档支持。\n少量响应被标记为违反政策。\n您需要评估每个问题。\n您应该使用哪些可观察信号来处理每个问题？要回答，请将适当的可观察信号拖到正确的问题上。每个可观察信号可以使用一次、使用多次或根本不使用。\n您可能需要拖动窗格之间的分隔条或滚动以查看内容。\n注意： 每个正确的选择值为一分。\n选择和放置：",
  "stemEn": "You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a customer support agent grounded in internal documentation.\nAfter a recent update, users report the following issues:\nSome answers are unsupported by retrieved documents.\nA small number of responses are flagged for policy violations.\nYou need to evaluate each issue.\nWhich observability signals should you use for each issue? To answer, drag the appropriate observability signals to the correct issues. Each observability signal may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.\nSelect and Place:",
  "explanationZh": "框 1：基础性评估指标\n一些答案没有被检索到的文档支持。\n要验证代理答案中的哪些声明没有得到您检索的内部文档的支持，您需要使用基础性（或忠实性）可观察信号。它专门设计用于通过验证生成的响应是否与提供的上下文在事实上一致来检测 AI 幻觉。\n该指标评估代理人回答中可以直接通过检索到的源上下文验证的索赔比例。\n随着时间推移，跟踪该指标作为一个聚合的指标信号将告诉您在最近更新后，问题在所有用户会话中的普遍程度。\n框 2：风险和安全指标\n少量响应被标记为违反政策。\n风险和安全指标是最佳选择。\n由于最近的更新特别触发了内容政策违规，这些评估者使用专门的 LLM-judge 指标（例如，内容过滤、自我伤害、仇恨、暴力和越狱检测）来诊断究竟是哪些短语或数据交互导致平台阻止代理的响应。\n直接对齐：政策违规直接属于人工智能安全、内容过滤和合规对齐的领域。\n针对性监控：在 Microsoft Foundry 中，风险和安全指标跟踪内容过滤日志、越狱尝试或政策不合规问题。这使您能够准确找出哪些响应被阻止以及原因（例如，特定过滤器如仇恨言论或暴力）。\nsources-a\nmonitoring-and-tracing-in-microsoft-foundry/4502760",
  "explanationEn": "Box 1: The Groundedness evaluation metric\nSome answers are unsupported by retrieved documents.\nTo verify which claims in the agent's answers are unsupported by your retrieved internal documents, you need to use the Groundedness (or Faithfulness) observability signal. It is specifically designed to detect AI hallucinations by verifying if the generated response is factually consistent with the provided context. This metric evaluates the fraction of claims in the agent’s answer that can be directly verified by the retrieved source context.\nTracking this metric as a aggregated Metric signal over time will tell you how widespread the issue is across all user sessions following the recent update.\nBox 2: Risk and safety metrics\nA small number of responses are flagged for policy violations.\nRisk and safety metrics is the best choice.\nBecause the recent update specifically triggers content policy violations, these evaluators use specialized LLM-judge metrics (e.g., content filters, self-harm, hate, violence, and jailbreak detection) to diagnose exactly which phrases or data interactions are causing the platform to block the agent’s responses.\nDirect Alignment: Policy violations directly fall under the domain of AI safety, content filtering, and compliance alignment.\nTargeted Monitoring: In Microsoft Foundry, Risk and safety metrics track content filtering logs, jailbreak attempts, or policy non-compliance issues. This allows you to pinpoint exactly which responses were blocked and why (e.g., specific filters like hate speech or violence).\nsources-a\nmonitoring-and-tracing-in-microsoft-foundry/4502760",
