  "explanation": "az cognitiveservices account show\n管理 Azure 认知服务账户。\n示例\n显示账户信息。\naz cognitiveservices account show --name myresource --resource-group cognitive-services-resource-group\n不正确：\n* az cognitiveservices account network-rule\n管理网络规则。\n* az resource link\n管理资源之间的链接。\n链接是资源管理器的一个功能。它允许声明资源之间的关系，即使它们不在同一个资源组中。链接对资源使用、计费或基于角色的访问没有影响。它允许将跨组的多个资源作为一个单元进行管理。\n* az account list\n获取已登录账户的订阅列表。默认情况下，仅显示当前云中的“启用”订阅。",
  "caseStudy": false,
  "answerConfidence": "medium",
  "answerFixed": false,
  "stemZh": "您有一个名为 Pipeline1 的 Azure DevOps 管道，用于部署应用程序。Pipeline1 包含一个将创建 Azure AI 服务帐户的步骤。\n您需要向 Pipeline1 添加一个步骤，以识别创建的 Azure AI 服务帐户。解决方案必须最小化开发工作量。\n您应该运行哪个 Azure 命令行界面 (CLI) 命令？",
  "stemEn": "You have an Azure DevOps pipeline named Pipeline1 that is used to deploy an app. Pipeline1 includes a step that will create an Azure AI services account.\nYou need to add a step to Pipeline1 that will identify the created Azure AI services account. The solution must minimize development effort.\nWhich Azure Command-Line Interface (CLI) command should you run?",
  "explanationZh": "az cognitiveservices account show\n管理 Azure 认知服务账户。\n示例\n显示账户信息。\naz cognitiveservices account show --name myresource --resource-group cognitive-services-resource-group\n不正确：\n* az cognitiveservices account network-rule\n管理网络规则。\n* az resource link\n管理资源之间的链接。\n链接是资源管理器的一个功能。它允许声明资源之间的关系，即使它们不在同一个资源组中。链接对资源使用、计费或基于角色的访问没有影响。它允许将跨组的多个资源作为一个单元进行管理。\n* az account list\n获取已登录账户的订阅列表。默认情况下，仅显示当前云中的“启用”订阅。",
  "explanationEn": "az cognitiveservices account show\nManage Azure Cognitive Services accounts.\nExample\nShow account information.\naz cognitiveservices account show --name myresource --resource-group cognitive-services-resource-group\nIncorrect:\n* az cognitiveservices account network-rule\nManage network rules.\n* az resource link\nManage links between resources.\nLinking is a feature of the Resource Manager. It enables declaring relationships between resources even if they do not reside in the same resource group. Linking has no impact on resource usage, billing, or role-based access. It allows for managing multiple resources across groups as a single unit.\n* az account list\nGet a list of subscriptions for the logged in account. By default, only 'Enabled' subscriptions from the current cloud is shown.",
