  "stemZh": "您有一个包含已部署聊天模型的 Microsoft Foundry 项目。\n您有一个 Python 服务，该服务向模型发送 API 请求。该服务与一个自动化验证系统集成，该系统将生成的输出与批准的响应模式进行比较。\n利益相关者报告说，小的措辞差异导致验证不匹配。\n您需要更新请求参数以提高输出稳定性。解决方案必须最大化推理质量。\n您应该如何完成 Python 代码？要回答，请在答案区域选择适当的选项。\n注意： 每个正确的选择值为一分。",
  "stemEn": "You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a deployed chat model.\nYou have a Python service that sends API requests to the model. The service is integrated with an automated validation system that compares generated outputs against approved response patterns.\nStakeholders report that small wording differences are causing validation mismatches.\nYou need to update the request parameters to improve output stability. The solution must maximize reasoning quality.\nHow should you complete the Python code? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
  "explanationZh": "框 1: 0\n最佳温度配置为 0。\n为什么温度 0 是最佳选择\n最大化可预测性：将温度设置为 0 使模型确定性。减少不匹配：它始终选择最可能的标记。这最小化了导致您验证失败的小措辞差异。\n保持推理能力：降低温度不会降低模型的核心推理能力；它只是消除了推理措辞中的随机变化。\n为什么其他选项失败\n温度 1：这是默认的创造性平衡。它允许标准标记变异，这将继续触发您的模式匹配不匹配。\n温度 2：这会产生最大随机性。输出将变得混乱、无意义，并完全破坏您的验证系统和推理质量。\n框 2: \"高\"\n高输出努力是此场景的最佳配置。\n为什么高努力是最佳选择\n最大化推理：高努力为内部思维链处理分配更多计算令牌。\n提高一致性：更好的推理帮助模型严格遵循您定义的复杂规则和批准的响应模式。\n减少边缘情况：微妙的措辞偏差通常发生在模型在没有充分规划的情况下匆忙生成时。",
  "explanationEn": "Box 1: 0\nThe best configuration for the temperature is 0.\nWhy Temperature 0 is Best\nMaximizes Predictability: Setting temperature to 0 makes the model deterministic.Reduces Mismatches: It always selects the most likely tokens. This minimizes the small wording differences causing your validation failures.\nPreserves Reasoning: Lowering temperature does not degrade the core reasoning capability of a model; it simply eliminates random variations in how that reasoning is phrased.\nWhy Other Options Fail\nTemperature 1: This is the default creative balance. It allows standard token variance, which will continue to trigger your pattern-matching mismatches.\nTemperature 2: This creates maximum randomness. The output will become chaotic, nonsensical, and completely break both your validation system and reasoning quality.\nBox 2: \"high\"\nHigh output effort is the best configuration for this scenario.\nWhy High Effort is Best\nMaximizes Reasoning: High effort allocates more computational tokens for internal chain-of-thought processing.\nImproves Consistency: Better reasoning helps the model strictly adhere to the complex rules and approved response patterns you have defined.\nReduces Edge Cases: Subtle wording deviations usually happen when a model rushes its generation without sufficient planning.",
  "domainLabelZh": "实现生成式 AI 与智能体解决方案",
  "domainLabelEn": "Implement generative AI and agentic solutions",
  "control": "select",
  "template": "message = client.messages.create(\n    model=\"deployment-name\",\n    messages=[\n        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Summarize the release notes in 3 bullet points.\"}\n    ],\n    max_tokens=800,\n    temperature={{1}},\n    thinking={\"type\": \"enabled\"},\n    output_config={\"effort\": {{2}}}\n)",
