  "stemZh": "您需要推荐一个计划，通过使用 Microsoft Foundry Agent Service 创建一个客户支持代理。该代理必须满足以下要求：\n在多次对话中保留用户偏好。\n允许用户在聊天过程中通过直接上传文档提供上下文支持。\n您应该为每个需求推荐哪个 Foundry 功能？要回答，请在答案区域选择适当的选项。\n注意： 每个正确的选择值为一分。",
  "stemEn": "You need to recommend a plan to create a customer support agent by using the Microsoft Foundry Agent Service. The agent must meet the following requirements:\nRetain user preferences across multiple conversations.\nEnable users to provide contextual grounding by directly uploading documents during a chat.\nWhich Foundry capability should you recommend for each requirement? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
  "explanationZh": "框 1：使用持久存储的代理记忆\n在多次对话中保留用户偏好。\n要使基于 Microsoft Foundry Agent Service 构建的客户支持代理在多次不同对话中保留用户偏好，您必须实现平台的本地托管长期记忆系统。\n解决方案架构必须包括以下特定组件和配置：\n*-> 1. 专用长期记忆存储\n代理到存储映射：为您的客户支持代理提供一个专用的记忆存储，以建立清晰的知识边界。\n托管生命周期操作：依赖服务运行时自动管理偏好的异步提取、合并（合并重复项和解决冲突事实）和混合搜索检索。\n2. 用户范围分区（记忆范围）\n隔离库：为每次交互定义一个强制性的记忆范围。\n唯一标识符：将范围参数绑定到持久标识符，如客户的 Microsoft Entra ID 或自定义系统 UUID。这确保用户偏好被安全隔离，不会泄漏到其他客户的会话中。\n3. 双重内存类型\n框 2：文件搜索工具\n为了使用户能够在聊天过程中直接上传文档以实现实时上下文支持，您应该包含文件搜索工具。\n该内置工具专门设计用于增强代理从上传的文件或专有文档中获取知识。当用户在聊天线程中上传文档时，Foundry Agent Service文件搜索工具会自动处理该文件的提取、分块、嵌入和向量搜索，以动态支持代理的响应。\n不正确：\n* Azure AI 搜索\n虽然它是一个知识支持工具，但 Azure AI 搜索工具旨在将代理连接到一个预先存在的集中式企业搜索索引。它不直接处理在聊天会话中临时用户文件的上传。\n* 代码解释器\n代码解释器工具用于在沙盒环境中执行 Python 代码，以进行高级数学计算、数据分析和图表生成，而不是文档向量检索。",
  "explanationEn": "Box 1: Agent memory that uses persistent storage\nRetain user preferences across multiple conversations.\nTo enable a customer support agent built on the Microsoft Foundry Agent Service to retain user preferences across multiple distinct conversations, you must implement the platform's native managed long-term memory system.\nThe solution architecture must include the following specific components and configurations:\n*-> 1. Dedicated Long-Term Memory Store\nAgent-to-Store Mapping: Provision one dedicated memory store attached directly to your customer support agent to establish a clear knowledge boundary.\nManaged Lifecycle Operations: Rely on the service runtime to automatically manage the asynchronous extraction of preferences, consolidation (merging duplicates and resolving conflicting facts), and hybrid\nsearch retrieval.\n2. User-Scoped Partitioning (Memory Scope)\nIsolation Vaults: Define a mandatory Memory Scope for every interaction.\nUnique Identifiers: Bind the scope parameter to a persistent identifier like the customer’s Microsoft Entra ID or a custom system UUID. This ensures user preferences are securely isolated and do not leak into other customers' sessions.\n3. Dual Memory Types\nBox 2: File Search tool\nTo enable users to directly upload documents during a chat for real-time contextual grounding, you should include the File Search tool.\nThis built-in tool is specifically designed to augment agents with knowledge from uploaded files or proprietary documents. When users upload a document during a chat thread, the Foundry Agent Service File Search Tool automatically handles the extraction, chunking, embedding, and vector searching of that file to ground the agent's responses dynamically.\nIncorrect:\n* Azure AI Search\nWhile it is a knowledge grounding tool, the Azure AI Search Tool is built to connect an agent to a pre-existing, centralized corporate search index. It does not handle ad-hoc user file uploads directly inside a chat session.\n* Code Interpreter\nThe Code Interpreter Tool is used for executing Python code in a sandboxed environment to perform advanced mathematical calculations, data analysis, and chart generation, rather than document vector retrieval.",
