  "stemZh": "您有一个包含代理的 Microsoft Foundry 项目。\n您使用 GitHub Actions 工作流进行 CI/CD。\n您需要配置工作流，以便在创建拉取请求 (PR) 时自动评估代理，并在评估结果未达到定义的阈值时阻止分支合并。\n您应该如何配置工作流？要回答，请在答案区域选择适当的选项。\n注意： 每个正确的选择值为一分。",
  "stemEn": "You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.\nYou use a GitHub Actions workflow for CI/CD.\nYou need to configure the workflow to automatically evaluate the agent when a pull request (PR) is created and prevent branches from merging if the evaluation results do NOT meet the defined thresholds.\nHow should you configure the workflow? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
  "explanationZh": "框 1：一个使用 OpenID Connect(OIDC) 的 Azure 登录操作。\n此场景最合适的身份验证方法是使用 OpenID Connect (OIDC) 的 Microsoft Entra ID 身份验证。\n使用 OIDC 和 azure/login GitHub Action 消除了在 GitHub 秘密中存储长期凭据（如密码或客户端密钥）的需要，提供了高度安全且无密码的集成。\n为什么 OIDC 是推荐的选择\n短期令牌：GitHub Actions 为每个工作流运行动态请求来自 Microsoft Entra ID 的临时范围令牌。\n无秘密轮换：消除了与管理长期存在的 Azure 服务主体秘密相关的管理开销和安全风险。\n细粒度 RBAC：通过将 Azure AI 用户角色分配给特定的存储库/工作流身份，可以严格限制权限，达到 Microsoft Foundry 资源级别。\n框 2：失败\n配置 GitHub Actions 工作流以在未满足阈值时以非零状态代码（失败）退出是阻止拉取请求的标准机制。要强制执行此限制，您必须将工作流配置与 GitHub 存储库设置配对。\n示例代码：\n- 名称：强制阈值\n运行：|\n# 使用 node、python 或 bash 读取 JSON 并验证\npython -c \"\n导入 json, sys\nwith open('results.json') as f:\ndata = json.load(f)\n如果 data['groundedness'] < 0.85:\nprint('错误：基础分数低于 0.85 阈值。')\nsys.exit(1)",
  "explanationEn": "Box 1: An Azure Login action that uses OpenID Connect(OIDC).\nThe most appropriate authentication method for this scenario is Microsoft Entra ID authentication using OpenID Connect (OIDC).\nUsing OIDC with the azure/login GitHub Action eliminates the need to store long-lived credentials (like passwords or client secrets) inside GitHub secrets, offering a highly secure and passwordless integration.\nWhy OIDC Is the Recommended Choice\nShort-Lived Tokens: GitHub Actions requests a temporary, scoped token from Microsoft Entra ID dynamically for each workflow run.\nNo Secret Rotations: Eliminates administrative overhead and safety risks associated with managing long-lived Azure Service Principal secrets.\nGranular RBAC: Permissions can be tightly scoped by assigning the Azure AI User role to the specific repository/workflow identity at the Microsoft Foundry resource level.\nBox 2: Fail\nConfiguring the GitHub Actions workflow to exit with a non-zero status code (fail) when thresholds are not met is the standard mechanism to block pull requests.To enforce this restriction, you must pair the workflow configuration with GitHub repository settings.\nExample code:\n- name: Enforce Thresholds\n run: |\n # Use node, python, or bash to read JSON and validate\n python -c \"\n import json, sys\n with open('results.json') as f:\n data = json.load(f)\n if data['groundedness'] < 0.85:\n print('Error: Groundedness score below 0.85 threshold.')\n sys.exit(1)",
  "domainLabelZh": "实现生成式 AI 与智能体解决方案",
  "domainLabelEn": "Implement generative AI and agentic solutions",
  "control": "select",
