  "explanation": "通过在提示中添加类似 // function F 是做什么的？的注释，您指示 GPT 模型提供对该函数行为的解释。这种方法直接要求模型解释代码，这将有助于生成解释，而无需对模型进行更改或额外的资源密集型配置。",
  "caseStudy": false,
  "answerConfidence": "medium",
  "answerFixed": false,
  "stemZh": "在 Microsoft Foundry 中，您使用带有 GPT-35 Turbo 模型的聊天游乐场。\n您有一个包含以下代码的提示。\n```\nfunction F(n)\n{\nvar f = [0, 1];\nfor (var i = 2; i < n; i++) f[i] = f[i-1] + f[i-2];\nreturn f;\n}\n```\n您需要模型创建代码的解释。解决方案必须尽量降低成本。\n您应该怎么做？",
  "stemEn": "In Microsoft Foundry, you use the Chat playground with the GPT-35 Turbo model.\nYou have a prompt that contains the following code.\n```\nfunction F(n)\n{\nvar f = [0, 1];\nfor (var i = 2; i < n; i++) f[i] = f[i-1] + f[i-2];\nreturn f;\n}\n```\nYou need the model to create an explanation of the code. The solution must minimize costs.\nWhat should you do?",
  "explanationZh": "通过在提示中添加类似 // function F 是做什么的？的注释，您指示 GPT 模型提供对该函数行为的解释。这种方法直接要求模型解释代码，这将有助于生成解释，而无需对模型进行更改或额外的资源密集型配置。",
  "explanationEn": "By adding a comment like // what does function F do? to the prompt, you are instructing the GPT model to provide an explanation of the function's behavior. This approach directly asks the model to explain the code, which will help generate an explanation without requiring changes to the model or additional resource-intensive configurations.",
