  "stemZh": "您有一个包含代理的 Microsoft Foundry 项目。\n代理接受用户上传的截图，并使用多模态聊天模型。\n一些截图可能包含恶意嵌入文本。\n您需要防止提示注入攻击，并确保第三方内容被视为低信任。\n您应该如何配置文档攻击的提示保护？要回答，请在答案区域选择适当的选项。\n注意： 每个正确的选择值为一分。",
  "stemEn": "You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.\nThe agent accepts user-uploaded screenshots and uses a multimodal chat model.\nSome screenshots contain potentially malicious embedded text.\nYou need to prevent a prompt injection attack and ensure that third-party content is treated as lower trust.\nHow should you configure prompt shields for document attacks? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
  "explanationZh": "为了防止用户上传的截图中恶意嵌入文本的间接提示注入，提示保护操作必须设置为“阻止”，并应启用聚焦功能。\n框 1：将操作设置为阻止\n提示屏蔽操作\n推荐的 Azure AI Foundry 配置\n要在使用多模态聊天模型的 Microsoft Foundry 代理中处理不受信任的第三方内容，请按如下方式配置您的护栏和内容过滤器：\n1. 风险下拉选择：选择文档攻击。文档攻击针对嵌入在外部内容（如文档、图像或文件）中的隐藏指令。\n*-> 2. 提示屏蔽操作：将操作设置为阻止。虽然“注释”会标记漏洞以供后续处理，但“阻止”会在文本到达模型会话之前实时停止注入尝试。\n框 2：启用聚焦\n额外缓解措施\n3. 聚焦切换：启用聚焦。该技术转换不受信任的文本，以便为模型提供其来源的持续信号。它将提取的屏幕截图文本视为相对于系统提示的低信任，从而防止隐藏命令的执行。\nintroducing/4458404",
  "explanationEn": "To prevent indirect prompt injection from malicious embedded text in user-uploaded screenshots, the Prompt Shield action must be set to \"block\" and Spotlighting should be enabled.\nBox 1: Set action to block\nPrompt shield action\nRecommended Azure AI Foundry Configuration\nTo handle untrusted, third-party content within a Microsoft Foundry agent using a multimodal chat model, configure your Guardrails and Content Filters as follows:\n1. Risk Dropdown Selection: Select Document attack. Document attacks target hidden instructions embedded in external content like documents, images, or files.\n*-> 2. Prompt Shield Action: Set the action to Block. While \"Annotate\" flags the vulnerability for downstream handling, \"Block\" stops the injection attempt in real-time before the text reaches the model session.\nBox 2: Enable spotlighting\nAdditional mitigation\n3. Spotlighting Toggle: Enable Spotlighting. This technique transforms untrusted text to give the model a continuous signal of its source. It treats the extracted screenshot text as lower trust relative to the system prompt, preventing hidden commands from executing.\nintroducing/4458404",
