  "stemZh": "您有一个应用程序，使用 Azure AI 自定义视觉和自定义训练的分类器来识别图像中的产品。\n您需要向分类器添加新产品。解决方案必须满足以下要求：\n● 尽量缩短添加产品所需的时间。\n● 最小化开发工作量。\n您应该按顺序执行哪五个操作？要回答，请将适当的操作从操作列表中移动到答案区域，并按正确顺序排列。\n选择和放置：",
  "stemEn": "You have an app that uses Azure AI Custom Vision and a custom trained classifier to identify products in images.\nYou need to add new products to the classifier. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n● Minimize how long it takes to add the products.\n● Minimize development effort.\nWhich five actions should you perform in sequence? To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.\nSelect and Place:",
  "explanationZh": "步骤 1：从 Visual Studio 打开项目\n使用 Visual Studio。例如：\n创建一个新的自定义模型\n首先，前往 Vision Studio 并选择图像分析选项卡。然后选择自定义模型tile。\n步骤 2：上传新产品的样本图像\n准备训练图像\n您需要将训练图像上传到 Azure Blob 存储容器。前往 Azure 门户中的存储资源并导航到存储浏览器选项卡。在这里，您可以创建一个 blob 容器并上传您的图像。将它们全部放在容器的根目录下。\n步骤 3：标记样本图像\n创建一个 Azure 机器学习标记项目\n您需要一个 COCO 文件来传达标记信息。生成 COCO 文件的简单方法是创建一个 Azure 机器学习项目，该项目附带数据标记工作流。\n在数据集详细信息页面，选择添加一个新的数据标注项目。为其命名并选择创建一个新的工作区。这将打开一个新的 Azure 门户标签页，在那里您可以创建 Azure 机器学习项目。\n步骤 4：重新训练模型\n步骤 5：发布模型",
  "explanationEn": "Step 1: From Visual Studio, open the project\nVisual Studio is used. For example:\nCreate a new custom model\nBegin by going to Vision Studio and selecting the Image analysis tab. Then select the Customize models tile.\nStep 2: Upload samples images of the new products\nPrepare training images\nYou need to upload your training images to an Azure Blob Storage container. Go to your storage resource in the Azure portal and navigate to the Storage browser tab. Here you can create a blob container and upload your images. Put them all at the root of the container.\nStep 3: Label the sample images\nCreate an Azure Machine Learning labeling project\nYou need a COCO file to convey the labeling information. An easy way to generate a COCO file is to create an Azure Machine Learning project, which comes with a data-labeling workflow.\nIn the dataset details page, select Add a new Data Labeling project. Name it and select Create a new workspace. That opens a new Azure portal tab where you can create the Azure Machine Learning project.\nStep 4: Retrain the model\nStep 5: Publish the model",
