  "stem": "您有一个包含代理的 Microsoft Foundry 项目。\n代理使用 Azure AI Search 进行检索增强生成 (RAG)。\n您计划摄取并索引 PDF 产品手册。\n您需要构建一个支持语义相似性匹配的解决方案。该解决方案必须确保在用户提问使用与产品手册不同的措辞时，代理能够检索到相关数据。\n您应该使用哪种索引方法？",
  "options": [
   {
    "id": "A",
    "text": "vector search",
    "textEn": "vector search",
    "textZh": "向量搜索"
   },
   {
    "id": "B",
    "text": "semantic ranking",
    "textEn": "semantic ranking",
    "textZh": "语义排名"
   },
   {
    "id": "C",
    "text": "suggesters",
    "textEn": "suggesters",
    "textZh": "建议者"
   },
   {
    "id": "D",
    "text": "analyzers",
    "textEn": "analyzers",
    "textZh": "分析器"
   }
  ],
  "answer": [
   "A"
  ],
  "pdfAnswer": [
   "A"
  ],
  "explanation": "向量搜索是此解决方案中正确的索引和检索类型。\n向量搜索与语义排名\n虽然这两种功能都有助于弥合不同措辞之间的差距，但向量搜索专门设计用于索引和检索层，以通过将文本转换为基于概念意义的数学向量（嵌入）来处理语义相似性匹配。语义排名是初始检索后应用的二次重新排名层，以提高精度，但它不能单独作为主要的索引方法。",
  "caseStudy": false,
  "answerConfidence": "medium",
  "answerFixed": false,
  "stemZh": "您有一个包含代理的 Microsoft Foundry 项目。\n代理使用 Azure AI Search 进行检索增强生成 (RAG)。\n您计划摄取并索引 PDF 产品手册。\n您需要构建一个支持语义相似性匹配的解决方案。该解决方案必须确保在用户提问使用与产品手册不同的措辞时，代理能够检索到相关数据。\n您应该使用哪种索引方法？",
  "stemEn": "You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.\nThe agent uses Azure AI Search for Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG).\nYou plan to ingest and index PDF product manuals.\nYou need to build a solution that supports semantic similarity matching. The solution must ensure that the agent retrieves relevant data when user questions use different wording than the product manuals.\nWhich indexing approach should you use?",
  "explanationZh": "向量搜索是此解决方案中正确的索引和检索类型。\n向量搜索与语义排名\n虽然这两种功能都有助于弥合不同措辞之间的差距，但向量搜索专门设计用于索引和检索层，以通过将文本转换为基于概念意义的数学向量（嵌入）来处理语义相似性匹配。语义排名是初始检索后应用的二次重新排名层，以提高精度，但它不能单独作为主要的索引方法。",
  "explanationEn": "Vector search is the correct indexing and retrieval type to use for this solution.\nVector search versus semantic ranking\nWhile both features help bridge the gap between different wordings, vector search is specifically designed at the indexing and retrieval layer to handle semantic similarity matching by converting text into mathematical vectors (embeddings) based on conceptual meaning. Semantic ranking is a secondary re-ranking layer applied after initial retrieval to improve precision, but it cannot function as the primary indexing method on its own.",
