  "stemZh": "您有一组存储为 PDF 文件的新闻稿。\n您需要从文件中提取文本并进行情感分析。\n您应该使用哪个服务来完成每个任务？要回答，请在答案区域选择适当的选项。\n注意： 每个正确的选择值为一分。",
  "stemEn": "You have a collection of press releases stored as PDF files.\nYou need to extract text from the files and perform sentiment analysis.\nWhich service should you use for each task? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
  "explanationZh": "框 1：Foundry Tools 中的 Azure 文档智能\nFoundry Tools 中的 Azure 文档智能现已普遍可用\n发布日期：2020 年 7 月 08 日\n宣布 Foundry Tools 中 Azure 文档智能的普遍可用版本发布。通过自动化信息提取，加速您的业务流程。\n您现在可以快速准确地从文档中提取文本、表格和键值对。只需几个样本，表单识别器就能根据您的文档进行定制理解，无论是在本地还是在云端。它支持多页文档（图像、PDF 和 Tiff 文件），并提取文档及其内容的结构化表示输出。\n不正确：\n* Foundry Tools 中的 Azure Vision\n计算机视觉 v4.0 读取 OCR（预览）是什么？\n新的计算机视觉图像分析 4.0 REST API 提供从图像中提取打印或手写文本的能力，采用统一的性能增强同步 API，使您能够轻松获取所有图像洞察，包括在单个 API 操作中的 OCR 结果。读取 OCR 引擎建立在多个深度学习模型之上，支持全球语言的通用脚本模型。\n框 2：Foundry Tools 中的 Azure 语言\n执行情感分析\n情感分析和意见挖掘是 Azure 语言认知服务提供的功能，这是一个用于开发涉及书面语言的智能应用程序的云端机器学习和 AI 算法集合。\noverview",
  "explanationEn": "Box 1: Azure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools\nAzure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools is now generally available\nPublished date: July 08, 2020\nAnnouncing the general availability release of Azure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools. Accelerate your business processes by automating information extraction.\nYou can now extract text, tables, and key value pairs quickly and accurately from documents. With just a few samples, Form Recognizer tailors its understanding to your documents, both on-premises and in the cloud. It supports multi-page documents (Images, PDFs and Tiff files) and extract a structured representation output of the document and its contents.\nIncorrect:\n* Azure Vision in Foundry Tools\nWhat is Computer Vision v4.0 Read OCR (preview)?\nThe new Computer Vision Image Analysis 4.0 REST API offers the ability to extract printed or handwritten text from images in a unified performance-enhanced synchronous API that makes it easy to get all image insights including OCR results in a single API operation. The Read OCR engine is built on top of multiple deep learning models supported by universal script-based models for global language support.\nBox 2: Azure Language in Foundry Tools\nPerform sentiment analysis\nSentiment analysis and opinion mining are features offered by Azure Cognitive Service for Language, a collection of machine learning and AI algorithms in the cloud for developing intelligent applications that involve written language.\noverview",
